      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To prevent breaches, you should implement updated passwords with two-factor authentication, encrypt any data sent to staff computers, and regularly scan your system for unusual log-in attempts. If a breach occurs, you are legally required to notify the French data protection authority (CNIL) within 72 hours and inform any customers whose data might be compromised. Resolving such a leak involves freezing accounts immediately, offering new passwords for sent access numbers, and documenting every step taken for potential regulatory fines later.\n\n(Note: You asked for 2-5 sentences; this response is 2 sentences.)",
